Below is a **step‑by‑step guide** (with ready‑to‑copy code) that shows how you can add a **keyboard‑typing animation** to any form field – for example, to animate a placeholder, a help tip, or even a “demo‑typing” preview of what the user will type.

---

## 1️⃣  What the animation does

| Element | What the animation shows |
|---------|--------------------------|
| **Placeholder / helper text** | Text appears character‑by‑character as if someone is typing it. |
| **Live‑typing preview** | While the user types, a ghost copy of the input is animated in sync (great for “demo” forms). |
| **Submit‑button feedback** | After the user clicks *Submit*, the button label can “type out” a thank‑you message. |

All of these can be built with the **SVG‑typing utilities** you already have:

* `createTypingSVG` – builds the SVG that will be animated.
* `setTypingAnimation` – controls speed & start delay.
* `customizeCursorStyle` – changes the cursor shape/color.
* `animateTextFormatting` – (optional) adds bold/italic/color changes while typing.

---

## 2️⃣  Basic HTML skeleton

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Form with Typing Animation</title>
  <style>
    /* Simple styling – feel free to adapt */
    .form-field {
      position: relative;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .typing-placeholder {
      position: absolute;
      left: 0.75rem;
      top: 0.5rem;
      pointer-events: none;               /* lets clicks go to the input */
      font-family: sans-serif;
      color: #777;
    }
    input, textarea {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-family: sans-serif;
    }
